    "derivedFromModernBorders": false,
    "geometryProvenance": "editorial_reconstruction",
    "justification": "Reusing a modern national boundary as a historical proxy is the failure this layer exists to avoid: it would make the Habsburg administration of Oltenia, or Moldavia before the Prut, invisible behind a line drawn in 1947. These rings are therefore drawn from the territorial record, declared editorial, given low confidence, and cut into phases at the instruments that actually moved the territory. They are envelopes for temporal filtering, not delimitations, and no vertex should be read as a claim about where a boundary ran on the ground.",
